{
  "duration": 421.8480000000115,
  "chapters": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 87.1200000000024
    },
    {
      "start": 87.1200000000024,
      "end": 167.83200000000457
    },
    {
      "start": 167.83200000000457,
      "end": 246.60000000000667
    },
    {
      "start": 246.60000000000667,
      "end": 329.4480000000089
    },
    {
      "start": 329.4480000000089,
      "end": 421.8480000000115
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1.399999976158142,
      "text": "Hey, welcome back.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 1.9199999570846558,
      "end": 5.139999866485596,
      "text": "We have simplified resistor networks and modeled real cells.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 5.659999847412109,
      "end": 9.319231033325195,
      "text": "Now we need a method that still works when several sources and branches",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 9.319231033325195,
      "end": 9.680000305175781,
      "text": "prevent",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 9.680000305175781,
      "end": 11.579999923706055,
      "text": "easy series or parallel reduction.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 11.579999923706055,
      "end": 14.539999961853027,
      "text": "Kirchhoff's first law is the junction rule.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 15.300000190734863,
      "end": 19.68000030517578,
      "text": "In a steady circuit, charge does not keep accumulating at a junction, so total",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 19.68000030517578,
      "end": 21.799999237060547,
      "text": "current entering equals total current leaving.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 22.5,
      "end": 24.579999923706055,
      "text": "This is charge conservation in action.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 25.34000015258789,
      "end": 29.420000076293945,
      "text": "Suppose five amperes enters a junction, while two amperes leaves along one",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 29.420000076293945,
      "end": 29.68000030517578,
      "text": "path.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 30.260000228881836,
      "end": 32.779998779296875,
      "text": "The remaining outgoing path carries three amperes.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 33.41999816894531,
      "end": 35.13999938964844,
      "text": "No current has been consumed at the node.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 35.939998626708984,
      "end": 39.7400016784668,
      "text": "Before solving an unfamiliar circuit, choose a current arrow for each branch.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 40.400001525878906,
      "end": 41.84000015258789,
      "text": "You are allowed to guess its direction.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 42.41999816894531,
      "end": 46.220001220703125,
      "text": "The arrow defines a positive reference; it does not guarantee the physical",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 46.220001220703125,
      "end": 46.619998931884766,
      "text": "result.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 47.279998779296875,
      "end": 52.040000915527344,
      "text": "If an equation returns minus one ampere, actual current is one ampere opposite",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 52.040000915527344,
      "end": 52.52000045776367,
      "text": "your arrow.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 53.2599983215332,
      "end": 56,
      "text": "Keep that negative sign when checking the original equations.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 56.599998474121094,
      "end": 60.13999938964844,
      "text": "Changing arrows halfway through without rewriting the equations creates",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 60.13999938964844,
      "end": 60.63999938964844,
      "text": "confusion.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 61.619998931884766,
      "end": 65.36000061035156,
      "text": "We assume steady direct current and ideal connecting wires in this class.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 66.12000274658203,
      "end": 69.81999969482422,
      "text": "For a connected circuit with several nodes, some junction equations repeat the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 69.81999969482422,
      "end": 70.5199966430664,
      "text": "same information.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 71.5199966430664,
      "end": 74.94000244140625,
      "text": "Usually one fewer independent junction equation than the number of nodes is",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 74.94000244140625,
      "end": 75.26000213623047,
      "text": "sufficient.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 76.27999877929688,
      "end": 79.95743551009741,
      "text": "Begin by tracing uninterrupted wires into nodes, then write the current",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 79.95743551009741,
      "end": 80.31999969482422,
      "text": "balance",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 80.31999969482422,
      "end": 81.62000274658203,
      "text": "at each independent junction.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 82.0199966430664,
      "end": 86.08000183105469,
      "text": "A complicated drawing becomes manageable when every current has a clear",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 86.08000183105469,
      "end": 86.80000305175781,
      "text": "reference direction.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 87.1200000000024,
      "end": 89.15999996185543,
      "text": "Kirchhoff's second law is the loop rule.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 89.67999994278195,
      "end": 91.92000019073727,
      "text": "Walk around a closed path and return to the same point.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 92.40000020981076,
      "end": 96.15999996185543,
      "text": "In our steady circuit model, the total signed change in electric potential is",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 96.15999996185543,
      "end": 96.47999965667965,
      "text": "zero.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 97.19999992370846,
      "end": 100.76000034332516,
      "text": "Sources supply energy per charge, and resistors transfer it into internal",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 100.76000034332516,
      "end": 101.15999996185543,
      "text": "energy.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 101.76000034332516,
      "end": 105.35999977112057,
      "text": "Choose a direction to walk around a loop; clockwise or counterclockwise both",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 105.35999977112057,
      "end": 105.66000091552975,
      "text": "work.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 106.19999992370846,
      "end": 108.4600001525903,
      "text": "This walking direction is separate from the current arrows.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 109.09999954223873,
      "end": 113.25999938965084,
      "text": "Across a resistor, walking with its reference current gives minus I R, a",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 113.25999938965084,
      "end": 113.8399993133569,
      "text": "potential drop.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 114.57999908447506,
      "end": 117.09999954223873,
      "text": "Walking against the reference arrow gives plus I R.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 117.09999954223873,
      "end": 121.14000045776608,
      "text": "Across an ideal source, walking from its negative terminal to its positive",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 121.14000045776608,
      "end": 122.48000061035397,
      "text": "terminal gives plus E.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 123.34000122070553,
      "end": 125.68000137329342,
      "text": "Walking from positive to negative gives minus E.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 126.30000030517819,
      "end": 129.59999954223872,
      "text": "Internal resistance is another resistor and follows the same resistor rule.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 130.5399981689477,
      "end": 134.45204973661222,
      "text": "Try one source of twelve volts, internal resistance one ohm and load five",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 134.45204973661222,
      "end": 134.71999847412349,
      "text": "ohms.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 135.59999954223872,
      "end": 138.29435768323307,
      "text": "Walking through the source from negative to positive, then with current",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 138.29435768323307,
      "end": 138.55999862671138,
      "text": "through",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 138.55999862671138,
      "end": 143.4399996948266,
      "text": "both resistances, gives twelve minus I times one minus I times five equals",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 143.4399996948266,
      "end": 143.73999893188716,
      "text": "zero.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 143.73999893188716,
      "end": 145.50000106811763,
      "text": "Current is two amperes.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 146.25999938965083,
      "end": 150.0200015258813,
      "text": "Reverse your entire walk and every sign reverses; the current solution remains",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 150.0200015258813,
      "end": 150.57999908447505,
      "text": "unchanged.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 151.07999908447505,
      "end": 152.88000213623286,
      "text": "That is a useful consistency check.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 153.67999755859614,
      "end": 157.74000274658442,
      "text": "This zero sum form assumes no changing magnetic flux supplies an unaccounted",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 157.74000274658442,
      "end": 158.60000335693599,
      "text": "induced EMF.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 159.39999877929927,
      "end": 161.21999847412349,
      "text": "Later, induction will extend the model.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 161.71999847412349,
      "end": 166.30000030517817,
      "text": "For now, mark polarities, draw current arrows and write each potential change",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 166.30000030517817,
      "end": 167.6200000000024,
      "text": "in the order you encounter it.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 167.83200000000457,
      "end": 170.75200007629851,
      "text": "Let's set up an original worked problem carefully.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 171.41199992371062,
      "end": 175.79200003815154,
      "text": "There are two nodes, A at the top and B at the bottom, with three branches",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 175.79200003815154,
      "end": 176.4320003814743,
      "text": "between them.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 176.99199984741668,
      "end": 181.04635905114657,
      "text": "The left branch has a twelve volt ideal source and a two ohm series",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 181.04635905114657,
      "end": 181.7120001144455,
      "text": "resistance.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 182.3119995422409,
      "end": 186.71199916077117,
      "text": "The right branch has a six volt ideal source and a two ohm series resistance.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 187.41199992371062,
      "end": 189.85200045776824,
      "text": "Both sources have their positive terminal toward A.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 190.2720005340622,
      "end": 192.49199984741668,
      "text": "The middle branch is a four ohm load.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 193.25200007629851,
      "end": 197.83200000000457,
      "text": "Choose I one upward from B to A in the left branch, I two upward in the right",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 197.83200000000457,
      "end": 200.33200000000457,
      "text": "branch, and I three downward through the load.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 200.85200045776824,
      "end": 204.8119995422409,
      "text": "At node A, write I one plus I two equals I three.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 204.8119995422409,
      "end": 208.6650137413714,
      "text": "Now walk from B upward through the left source branch and downward through the",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 208.6650137413714,
      "end": 208.91200183105926,
      "text": "load.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 209.471999389653,
      "end": 213.87199964396615,
      "text": "The source raises potential by twelve, its series resistor lowers it by two I",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 213.87199964396615,
      "end": 216.85200045776824,
      "text": "one, and the load lowers it by four I three.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 216.85200045776824,
      "end": 217.63199923706512,
      "text": "Their sum is zero.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 218.17200015259246,
      "end": 222.69200061035613,
      "text": "For the right loop, the same walk gives six minus two I two minus four I three",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 222.69200061035613,
      "end": 223.45199893188934,
      "text": "equals zero.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 223.79199908447723,
      "end": 227.2120010681198,
      "text": "We have three unknown branch currents and three independent equations.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 227.8119995422409,
      "end": 231.59199832153777,
      "text": "The loop across the two source branches would add no new information; it",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 231.59199832153777,
      "end": 233.8720009155319,
      "text": "follows by subtracting these two loop equations.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 234.83200000000457,
      "end": 239.0719978637741,
      "text": "Pause before solving and check the picture: source polarities, resistor values",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 239.21199725342254,
      "end": 241.93199847412566,
      "text": "and chosen current arrows must match every term.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 242.35199664307098,
      "end": 246.33200000000457,
      "text": "The six volt branch may turn out to absorb energy rather than supply it.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 246.33200000000457,
      "end": 246.60000000000667,
      "text": "Our signed equations will tell us.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 246.60000000000667,
      "end": 249.52000007630062,
      "text": "Let V be the potential of A relative to B.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 250.19999990463924,
      "end": 251.9800001144476,
      "text": "The load current is V divided by four.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 252.5000000953741,
      "end": 256.78000030518245,
      "text": "The left source current is twelve minus V divided by two, and the right source",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 256.78000030518245,
      "end": 259.37999973297786,
      "text": "current is six minus V divided by two.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 260.37999973297786,
      "end": 265.0400005340643,
      "text": "Substituting into the junction equation gives nine minus V equals V over four.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 265.7399993896551,
      "end": 269.05999908447933,
      "text": "Multiply by four: thirty six minus four V equals V.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 269.8800006866522,
      "end": 271.7399993896551,
      "text": "Therefore V is seven point two volts.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 271.7399993896551,
      "end": 276.6799999237127,
      "text": "I one becomes two point four amperes, I two becomes minus zero point six",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 276.6799999237127,
      "end": 279.53999862671566,
      "text": "amperes, and I three becomes one point eight amperes.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 280.37999877930355,
      "end": 284.78000030518245,
      "text": "The negative result is useful information: actual current in the six volt",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 284.78000030518245,
      "end": 288.3000007629461,
      "text": "branch travels from A to B, opposite our upward reference arrow.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 289.37999877930355,
      "end": 292.96000061035824,
      "text": "Current enters that source's positive terminal, so the ideal six volt source",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 292.96000061035824,
      "end": 293.71999893189144,
      "text": "absorbs energy.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 294.579999542243,
      "end": 298.19846291175924,
      "text": "Check the junction: two point four minus zero point six equals one point",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 298.19846291175924,
      "end": 298.5000015258856,
      "text": "eight.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 299.140000915534,
      "end": 302.6600013732977,
      "text": "Check the left loop: twelve minus four point eight minus seven point two is",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 302.6600013732977,
      "end": 302.8999992370672,
      "text": "zero.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 303.3999992370672,
      "end": 306.96000061035824,
      "text": "Check the right: six plus one point two minus seven point two is zero.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 307.8000007629461,
      "end": 308.69999847412777,
      "text": "Now verify power.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 308.87999877930355,
      "end": 311.68000183106136,
      "text": "The twelve volt source supplies twenty eight point eight watts.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 312.26000366211605,
      "end": 314.68000183106136,
      "text": "The six volt source absorbs three point six watts.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 315.5400024414129,
      "end": 319.019998168952,
      "text": "Resistor heating totals twenty five point two watts: eleven point five two in",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 319.019998168952,
      "end": 322.87999877930355,
      "text": "the left branch, zero point seven two in the right, and twelve point nine six",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 322.87999877930355,
      "end": 323.4399963378973,
      "text": "in the load.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 324.4000030517645,
      "end": 326.28000030518245,
      "text": "Absorption plus heating equals the supplied power.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 326.9199996948309,
      "end": 329.4480000000089,
      "text": "A negative current never makes resistor heating negative; use I squared R.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 329.4480000000089,
      "end": 333.36800007630285,
      "text": "Let's finish with a routine you can carry into a JEE problem.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 334.3280001144498,
      "end": 336.48799996186193,
      "text": "First label nodes by tracing ideal wires.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 337.567999885568,
      "end": 341.607999847421,
      "text": "Next mark every source polarity and choose one reference current per branch.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 342.5080004196256,
      "end": 345.607999847421,
      "text": "Write enough independent junction and loop equations for the unknowns.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 346.5079994659513,
      "end": 350.08799938965734,
      "text": "Solve the equations, interpret signs, and check the original circuit.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 350.607999847421,
      "end": 355.18799977112707,
      "text": "A branch containing a source cannot generally be merged with another branch by",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 355.18799977112707,
      "end": 357.2679996948331,
      "text": "using only the parallel resistor formula.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 357.8279991607755,
      "end": 361.6280003051847,
      "text": "Sources maintain their own potential rises and can oppose one another.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 362.5280018310636,
      "end": 365.48800091553625,
      "text": "Include each source and each internal resistance explicitly.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 366.8679981689542,
      "end": 371.3879986267179,
      "text": "For an ideal ammeter, resistance is zero; placing it between two nodes can",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 371.3879986267179,
      "end": 373.5280018310636,
      "text": "change the circuit by joining their potentials.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 374.3480015258878,
      "end": 378.3095389603924,
      "text": "For an ideal voltmeter, resistance is infinite and no current flows through",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 378.3095389603924,
      "end": 378.4680004577726,
      "text": "its",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 378.4680004577726,
      "end": 378.7679996948331,
      "text": "branch.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 379.4680004577726,
      "end": 383.04799847413,
      "text": "A voltmeter reading of zero does not automatically mean there is no current",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 383.04799847413,
      "end": 383.5280018310636,
      "text": "elsewhere.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 384.1880016784757,
      "end": 386.3679981689542,
      "text": "Keep meter connections in the diagram while reasoning.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 386.3679981689542,
      "end": 390.7880001525968,
      "text": "If you get a negative branch current, retain it in the equations and describe",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 390.7880001525968,
      "end": 391.82800106812414,
      "text": "the actual direction.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 392.8879986267179,
      "end": 396.48800091553625,
      "text": "Check resistor heating with current squared times resistance, and determine",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 396.48800091553625,
      "end": 400.1479969482511,
      "text": "source power from whether current leaves or enters the positive terminal.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 401.1280003051847,
      "end": 404.50799755860265,
      "text": "More elaborate circuits use the same method with more independent equations.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 405.38800244141515,
      "end": 409.06800274659093,
      "text": "Bridges will be our next application, where equal potentials can make a",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 409.06800274659093,
      "end": 410.4280033569425,
      "text": "connecting branch carry zero current.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 410.7279987793058,
      "end": 414.6479969482511,
      "text": "For today's class, the important skill is not guessing which source wins.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 414.9280033569425,
      "end": 419.3279972534269,
      "text": "It is translating a clearly labeled circuit into consistent signed equations",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 419.3279972534269,
      "end": 421.54799847413,
      "text": "and letting those equations answer the question.",
      "chapter": 4
    }
  ]
}
